   You find at the counter of what you discover is a chateau-turned-hotel. 
From behind the counter, a spectacled old woman greets you in a thick accent.

   "Velcome! Velcome, to Karnstein Chateau. Mein goodness, vee have 
such distinvished guests and dear me, on such an evening. Vell no matter, 
but vee must hurry you in here, and close zhose doors." says Oma. 

   "If you'll excuse me for a moment, I'll prepare zhe kitchen for your 
arrival. Vhen all of your party has arrived, if you vill ring zhe bell, 
ve vill show you and your party to your rooms." the old woman smiles briefly
and scurries off.
